--   A shifted Fresnel integral on a diagonal line
-- statement:
--   For real $c$, complex $B$, and $L_+(c,F)=\int_{\mathbb R}F(c+v(1+i))(1+i)\,dv$,
--
--   $$L_+\!\left(c,z\mapsto e^{\pi i(z+B)^2}\right)=e^{\pi i/4}.$$
--
--   This evaluates the diagonal Gaussian integral used at the saddle point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/RS_Kernel.lean#L274-L294

